---@class cloudflare.iam.PatchOauthClientRequest
---@field account_id string Account identifier tag.
---@field oauth_client_id string The unique identifier for an OAuth client.
---@field allowed_cors_origins? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestAllowedCorsOriginsList Array of allowed CORS origins.
---@field client_name? string Human-readable name of the OAuth client.
---@field client_uri? string URL of the home page of the client.
---@field grant_types? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestGrantTypesList Array of OAuth grant types the client is allowed to use. `authorization_code` is required; `refresh_token` may be included optionally.
---@field logo_uri? string URL of the client's logo.
---@field optional_scopes? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestOptionalScopesList Scopes that the authorizing user may decline during consent. Each value must also appear in `scopes`. The scopes `openid`, `offline`, and `offline_access` cannot be optional.
---@field policy_uri? string URL that points to a privacy policy document.
---@field post_logout_redirect_uris? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestPostLogoutRedirectUrisList Array of allowed post-logout redirect URIs.
---@field redirect_uris? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestRedirectUrisList Array of allowed redirect URIs for the client.
---@field response_types? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestResponseTypesList Array of OAuth response types the client is allowed to use.
---@field scopes? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestScopesList Array of OAuth scopes the client is allowed to request. Colon-delimited scopes are not accepted. Dot-delimited scopes are validated against available OAuth API scopes; simple identity scopes are allowed. Protocol scopes `offline_access` and `openid` are added or removed automatically based on `grant_types` and `response_types`.
---@field token_endpoint_auth_method? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestTokenEndpointAuthMethod|string The authentication method the client uses at the token endpoint.
---@field tos_uri? string URL that points to a terms of service document.
---@field visibility? cloudflare.iam.OauthClientsUpdateRequestVisibility|string Promote the OAuth client from private to public visibility. Only `public` is accepted; demotion to `private` is not supported. Promotion requires a non-empty client name, logo URI, verified client URI host, and at least one non-identity scope.

---Unwrapped `result` payload of the Cloudflare v4 response envelope.
